## environment analysis of the 5 integration failures in 04-integration.log (20:26:04)
Cause: the clone's per-package node_modules shim linked @mth/* to the repository's own workspace links, which resolve to /home/user/My-owns/packages/* (the stack in 04-integration.log shows renderPdf at ../../../../../home/user/My-owns/packages/reporting/src/pdf/index.ts). The test files import RenderError by relative path from the clone (exports.test.ts l.16), while apps/worker/src/reports/export-runner.ts imports it via @mth/reporting; two module instances -> 'err instanceof RenderError' (export-runner.ts l.462) is false -> the job is not failed with export.render_failed. contract.test.ts and response-validation.test.ts fail in their P5 BE-M exercise for the same reason, and their coverage assertion then lists cancelExport (exercised only after that point) as never successful.
Fix (mine): each @mth link replaced by a real directory with relative links into the clone; re-run of the 3 files: 246/246 pass, exit 0 (04b-integration-rerun.log).

## which compiled package code the e2e stacks ran
The repository tree equals the candidate (git diff 7579382c HEAD touches only docs/delivery; candidate id recomputed). Compiled package output (JS and JSON files under packages/*/dist), repository vs clone build of 7579382c:
  config repo 68e32dcec34e3877 clone 68e32dcec34e3877 EQUAL
  db repo 34c3bb4cd25d2ad5 clone 34c3bb4cd25d2ad5 EQUAL
  design-tokens repo e465877b184ead8b clone e465877b184ead8b EQUAL
  reporting repo 61b2e504c477f8b3 clone 61b2e504c477f8b3 EQUAL
  shared repo 92599fd3a9c31ef5 clone 92599fd3a9c31ef5 EQUAL
So the product e2e runs (en, ar, demo keyboard), which started with the old shim, executed the same compiled code as the candidate build. Unit tests resolve @mth/* to src via the @mth/source condition, and the repository src equals the candidate src. The root acceptance run started at ~20:05 with the old shim, and the links were changed at 20:22 while it ran; both targets hold identical content. The A18 and A19 drills build and install from the clone's git commit, independent of the shim.
